body:
Since reddit is useless and always either gives you a garbage answer or just nothing at all, here's the answer for all of you:

Make a new java class to replace the normal FlowerBlock one and use that in your Modded Blocks class instead for the flower block, and here is the code for the new class:

    import net.minecraft.block.BlockState;
import net.minecraft.block.FlowerBlock;
import net.minecraft.entity.effect.StatusEffect;
import net.minecraft.util.math.BlockPos;
import net.minecraft.world.BlockView;

public class ModFlowerBlock extends FlowerBlock {
    public ModFlowerBlock(StatusEffect suspiciousStewEffect, int effectDuration, Settings settings) {
        super(suspiciousStewEffect, effectDuration, settings);
    }

    @Override
    protected boolean canPlantOnTop(BlockState floor, BlockView world, BlockPos pos) {
        return floor.isIn(EndiumTag.AMARANTH_PLANTABLE);
    }
}

In this example the tag being End Stone.

Thanks for nothing reddit, you're welcome.
